{"assets":["/statement-assets/4e4962f09355765b303109fe9c422aca338cb0268dfb67d0d8aa91811883a282.png","/statement-assets/68196683be30e6910599612856901dd5bcef66837ce39dd132dee90172f2e6d8.png"],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"999","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"E. Reachability from the Capital"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"},{"kind":"text","text":":"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"There are $$$n$$$ cities and $$$m$$$ roads in Berland. Each road connects a pair of cities. The roads in Berland are one-way."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"What is the minimum number of new roads that need to be built to make all the cities reachable from the capital?"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"New roads will also be one-way."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input consists of three integers $$$n$$$, $$$m$$$ and $$$s$$$ ($$$1 \\le n \\le 5000, 0 \\le m \\le 5000, 1 \\le s \\le n$$$) — the number of cities, the number of roads and the index of the capital. Cities are indexed from $$$1$$$ to $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The following $$$m$$$ lines contain roads: road $$$i$$$ is given as a pair of cities $$$u_i$$$, $$$v_i$$$ ($$$1 \\le u_i, v_i \\le n$$$, $$$u_i \\ne v_i$$$). For each pair of cities $$$(u, v)$$$, there can be at most one road from $$$u$$$ to $$$v$$$. Roads in opposite directions between a pair of cities are allowed (i.e. from $$$u$$$ to $$$v$$$ and from $$$v$$$ to $$$u$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Print one integer — the minimum number of extra roads needed to make all the cities reachable from city $$$s$$$. If all the cities are already reachable from $$$s$$$, print "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"0"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Examples"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"9 9 1\n1 2\n1 3\n2 3\n1 5\n5 6\n6 1\n1 8\n9 8\n7 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"3\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"5 4 5\n1 2\n2 3\n3 4\n4 1\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"1\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first example is illustrated by the following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/4e4962f09355765b303109fe9c422aca338cb0268dfb67d0d8aa91811883a282.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, you can add roads ($$$6, 4$$$), ($$$7, 9$$$), ($$$1, 7$$$) to make all the cities reachable from $$$s = 1$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second example is illustrated by the following:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"attrs":{"alt":"","src":"/statement-assets/68196683be30e6910599612856901dd5bcef66837ce39dd132dee90172f2e6d8.png"},"kind":"image"}],"kind":"container"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this example, you can add any one of the roads ($$$5, 1$$$), ($$$5, 2$$$), ($$$5, 3$$$), ($$$5, 4$$$) to make all the cities reachable from $$$s = 5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"E","problemCode":"999E","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/999/problem/E"}